#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|title=The Baritone Voice: A Personal Guide to Acquiring a Superior Singing Technique|author=S. Anthony Frisella|url= https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/The_Baritone_Voice/4wNVqRG99b4C?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=cross+the+break+voice+sing&pg=PT14&printsec=frontcover|page=14|passage=The point of division between the two vocal registers is most frequently referred to as the ''register’s '''break'''''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|title=The Evolving Singing Voice: Changes Across the Lifespan|author=Karen Brunssen|url= https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/The_Evolving_Singing_Voice/phKGDwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=cross+the+break+voice+sing&pg=PA76&printsec=frontcover|page=76|passage=Boys should continue in their high voice, across the '''break''' to the lower range, and end up with a voice that doesn’t have a '''break''' (Leck, 2009).}}
